{"id":"create-cracklib-dict.8","n":"create-cracklib-dict","s":"8","src":{"r":{"pkg":"cracklib","ver":"2.9.6-27.el9","repo":"BaseOS","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/BaseOS/x86_64/os/Packages/c/cracklib-2.9.6-27.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/create-cracklib-dict.8.gz","sha256":"05abbfe7039c63fd1f3e9c216beec6edfda60568ee2f12e203f126dd2b618877","date":"Sat Jun 21 22:45:42 CEST 2008","origin":"Jan Dittberner"},"u":{"pkg":"cracklib-runtime","ver":"2.9.6-3.4build4","repo":"jammy/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/c/cracklib2/cracklib-runtime_2.9.6-3.4build4_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/create-cracklib-dict.8.gz","sha256":"e720106c99a182de949afc18521c4025887d0e3d5751e034fae2bc16db9716d6","date":"Sat Jun 21 22:45:42 CEST 2008","origin":"Jan Dittberner"}},"nopt":{"r":0,"u":0},"desc":"Check passwords using libcrack2","same":true,"doc":[["NAME","<p>create-cracklib-dict - Check passwords using libcrack2</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>create-cracklib-dict wordlist ...</b></p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>create-cracklib-dict</b> takes one or more word list files as arguments and converts them into cracklib dictionaries for use by password checking programs. The results are placed in the default compiled-in dictionary location.</p> <p>If you wish to store the dictionary in a different location, use the cracklib-format and cracklib-packer commands directly.</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>cracklib-format</b>(8), <b>cracklib-packer</b>(8), <b>cracklib-check</b>(8),</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p>This man page was written by Jan Dittberner &lt;jandd@debian.org&gt; for the Debian GNU/Linux System (but may be used by others).</p>"]]}